`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Where the model's sensitivity itself is honest and where it is not"}),": below the point where knock intrudes, this simulator's efficiency gain per unit of compression is somewhat steeper than the ideal Otto relation predicts (roughly 20% measured against roughly 11.5% ideal, moving from CR 8 to CR 12). Teach the ",e.jsx(t.em,{children:"shape and the ceiling"})," from this experiment — both are correct and reproducible. Treat the exact slope as this simulator's calibration, not a universal number."]}),`
