`,e.jsx(t.h2,{children:"Frequently Asked Questions"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{children:"Does a rotary engine have pistons or valves?"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"No. A triangular rotor replaces the pistons, and ports in the housing replace poppet valves. The rotor uncovers and covers the ports as it turns, so port position sets the timing."}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{children:"How many power pulses does a rotary engine make?"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["One per rotor per shaft turn. The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://dieselnet.com/tech/engine_alternatives.php",children:"shaft turns three times per rotor revolution and there are three power pulses in that revolution"}),". A two-rotor therefore pulses twice per shaft turn, the same as a four-cylinder four-stroke. The simulator counted 180 fire events in 90 turns on its two-rotor."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{children:"Is a rotary engine a two-stroke?"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["No. Each chamber runs four separate processes, intake, compression, combustion and exhaust, at 270° of shaft each. It shares a ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"/blog/two-stroke-vs-four-stroke",children:"two-stroke's"})," ports and its pulse rate of one per turn, which is where the comparison comes from."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{children:"Are rotary engines smoother than piston engines?"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"In torque, yes, in our model. At two pulses per turn and 4,000 rpm, peak torque is 2.31× the mean on the two-rotor against 3.75× on the inline-four. The model has no reciprocating inertia or vibration output, so it cannot measure how much either engine shakes."}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{children:"Does Mazda still make rotary engines?"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Its most recent rotary is the 8C, an ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://uk.mazda-press.com/news/2023/mazda-mx-30-e-skyactiv-r-ev-revealed-at-brussels-motor-show-----------------------------uk-pricing-and-specification-announced/",children:"830 cc single rotor"})," used as a generator in the MX-30 R-EV. In January 2026 ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://www.electrive.com/2026/01/14/mazda-discontinues-the-mx-30-r-ev-from-the-market",children:"electrive reported that car being phased out in Europe"}),", with Japanese production temporarily suspended. Mazda's ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://newsroom.mazda.com/en/publicity/release/2025/202510/251029b.html",children:"Vision X-Coupe"})," with a two-rotor rotary turbo is a concept."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h2,{children:"How These Numbers Were Made"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Every simulator figure comes from one headless run on 2026-11-05, repeated with byte-identical results. Peak figures are the 24-point dyno sweep the engine roster prints, and the port table uses the 40-point sweep the on-screen dyno runs. Ripple was measured at a held rpm, wide open, once the charge had settled: 1° steps over 12 full cycles folded onto one, with the display smoothing removed per step. As a control, the folded mean sits within 0.4% of a separately held average on every rotary and within 0.8% on the pistons printed here. Port idles ran for 10 seconds after a 10-second settle, and a burn counts as complete at 90% burnt by exhaust opening, misfire under 30%."}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"The model has limits. Chamber volume is one cosine harmonic of the true trochoid, and wall heat is one lumped coefficient. Combustion is a flat 0.75 of the fuel's heat, the spark is fixed at 15° before top dead centre at every rpm and load, and fuel is always stoichiometric gasoline, with no flame travel across the crescent. Ripple is gas torque less friction before any flywheel. We leave the model's full-throttle fuel figures out of this article because they run against the real engines. The 4-rotor's output comes from its race calibration, so it stays out of the per-litre comparisons."}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{children:"About this article"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Written by the team that builds the simulator and maintains its rotary model. The simulator numbers are the model's and are stated as such; the history, oil, seal and emissions material comes from the sources below, and each section says which is which."}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h2,{children:"Sources and Further Reading"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.ul,{children:[`
`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:[e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://patents.google.com/patent/US8985085B2/en",children:"US patent 8985085B2"})," (housing shape and working chambers, retrieved 2026-11-05)"]}),`
