`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Read the two Δ columns against each other. At every step they agree to within 0.1 point, from +2.85% on both engines at 8.5 → 9 to +1.62% and +1.61% at 13 → 13.5. The LS7 and the 4.6 share no geometry, no cam and no head; what they share is the Otto cycle. Per full point, that is about 5.6% at the bottom of the sweep and about 3.3% at the top."}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"The peaks hold still. The LS7's power peak sits at 5,875 rpm from 9.5:1 up and its torque peak at 4,525 until 13:1, where it drifts to 4,750; the 4.6's power peak stays at 5,054 until the last step. Compression raises the whole curve rather than reshaping it."}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{children:"The Ideal Cycle Beside the Measurement"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"The sanity check is whether the simulator is doing physics or a lookup. Take η = 1 − r^(1−γ) across each half-point step and compare the fractional change in efficiency with the fractional change in measured LS7 power, for the air-standard γ of 1.4 and for 1.3, closer to a fuel-air charge:"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.table,{children:[e.jsx(t.thead,{children:e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsx(t.th,{children:"Step"}),e.jsx(t.th,{children:"Δη/η, γ 1.4"}),e.jsx(t.th,{children:"Δη/η, γ 1.3"}),e.jsx(t.th,{children:"Measured Δhp/hp (LS7)"})]})}),e.jsxs(t.tbody,{children:[e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsx(t.td,{children:"8.5 → 9"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"+1.67%"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"+1.89%"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"+2.85%"})]}),e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsx(t.td,{children:"9 → 9.5"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"+1.52%"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"+1.72%"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"+2.68%"})]}),e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsx(t.td,{children:"9.5 → 10"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"+1.39%"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"+1.58%"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"+2.49%"})]}),e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsx(t.td,{children:"10 → 10.5"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"+1.28%"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"+1.46%"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"+2.33%"})]}),e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsx(t.td,{children:"10.5 → 11"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"+1.18%"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"+1.35%"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"+2.17%"})]}),e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsx(t.td,{children:"11 → 11.5"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"+1.09%"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"+1.26%"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"+2.04%"})]}),e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsx(t.td,{children:"11.5 → 12"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"+1.02%"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"+1.17%"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"+1.91%"})]}),e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsx(t.td,{children:"12 → 12.5"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"+0.95%"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"+1.10%"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"+1.81%"})]}),e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsx(t.td,{children:"12.5 → 13"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"+0.89%"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"+1.03%"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"+1.71%"})]}),e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsx(t.td,{children:"13 → 13.5"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"+0.84%"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"+0.97%"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"+1.62%"})]})]})]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The measured gain runs above the ideal-cycle gain at every step, by a steady margin, and the two decline together. Two things account for the margin. First, combustion here is a Wiebe burn spread over 60° of crank on the LS7, with heat transfer to the walls, not the instantaneous constant-volume heat release the ideal cycle assumes. Its efficiency sits below the ideal, and a cycle that starts lower gains a larger ",e.jsx(t.em,{children:"fraction"})," from the same improvement. Second, friction in this model is charged on mean piston speed, which compression does not change, so the friction bill is the same at 8.5:1 as at 13.5:1 and brake power moves by more than indicated power does. The ideal column is the textbook, not this model's prediction."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h2,{children:"The Sweep Again, Knock On"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Now put the fuel back. Same compression ladder, each point held wide open at 4,500 rpm for six seconds with torque averaged and knock read as the maximum over the last five of them, on 91, 93 and 98 octane. The index is our model's own intensity number: 0 is nothing, and 0.35 is what the gauge calls heavy knock. Below 11:1 every column is identical to the knock-free control on both engines and the index reads 0.0000 all the way down, so the tables start where something happens."}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"LS7, torque at 4,500 rpm:"}),`
